        "form": "10-K",
        "filed": "2026-09-03"
      },
      {
        "key": "variable_consideration",
        "label": "Variable consideration / rebates / returns",
        "excerpt": "cost and performance incentives and penalties that can either increase or decrease the contract price. These variable consideration amounts are generally earned or incurred based on certain performance metrics, most commonly related to project schedule or cost targets. Contracts",
        "classification": "unverified_text_lead",
        "source_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/866273/000086627326000057/mtrx-20260630.htm",
        "accession": "0000866273-26-000057",
        "form": "10-K",
        "filed": "2026-09-03"
      },
      {
        "key": "contract_modification",
        "label": "Contract modifications",
        "excerpt": "one of the most common forms of variable consideration included within contract value and typically represent contract modifications for which a change in scope has been authorized or acknowledged by our customer but the final adjustment to contract price is yet to be negotiated.",
        "classification": "unverified_text_lead",
        "source_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/866273/000086627326000057/mtrx-20260630.htm",
        "accession": "0000866273-26-000057",
        "form": "10-K",
        "filed": "2026-09-03"
      },
      {
        "key": "deferred_revenue",
        "label": "Deferred revenue / contract liabilities",
        "excerpt": "gs on Uncompleted Contracts (\"CIE\"). CIE consists of revenue recognized in excess of billings. We present our contract liabilities in the balance sheet as Billings on Uncompleted Contracts in Excess of Costs and Estimated Earnings (\"BIE\"). BIE consists of billings in excess of re",
